# Prove a risk BAND of a PRIVATE score, revealing only the band WORD, and the words have DIFFERENT
# Default proofs are sound but not zero-knowledge: add --zk to hide the private inputs.
# lengths. The branches of an `if`/`match` over strings need not be equal width (compare
# private_verdict.glass, whose four verdicts are all 4 letters):
# the bridge NUL-pads the shorter branch with a codepoint-0 sentinel and decode stops there, so
# the natural, varying-length words just lower, and the four nested `if`s here all differ in length.
#
#   glass prove examples/prove/private_risk.glass score=95   # -> "CRITICAL", ACCEPT
#   glass prove examples/prove/private_risk.glass score=70   # -> "HIGH",     ACCEPT
#   glass prove examples/prove/private_risk.glass score=40   # -> "MEDIUM",   ACCEPT
#   glass prove examples/prove/private_risk.glass score=10   # -> "LOW",      ACCEPT
#
# The band word is bound as the public result; the score it was computed from stays in the witness.
# The selected branch is the only thing revealed: the verifier learns the band, never the number.
# The cross-check (glass.py) recomputes the same word, confirming the circuit selected the band the
# source dictates, not a corrupted muxing of the branches.
fn classify(s: Int) : String =
  if s >= 90 then "CRITICAL"
  else if s >= 60 then "HIGH"
  else if s >= 30 then "MEDIUM"
  else "LOW"

classify(score)
